description:
validate_attachments() accepts degenerate content_type values like '/pdf' or 'text/' because it only checks that exactly one '/' exists, not that both sides are non-empty.

Fix: after counting slashes, also verify that the part before the slash is non-empty and the part after the slash is non-empty. E.g.:
  let parts: Vec<&str> = a.content_type.splitn(2, '/').collect();
  if parts.len() != 2 || parts[0].is_empty() || parts[1].is_empty() { reject }

File: crates/kith-peer/src/lib.rs — validate_attachments() around line 718-726.

Also add a test: deliver_attachment_degenerate_content_type_rejected (e.g., content_type='/plain' or 'text/').
